WHAT1='Nori, a sturdy chibi forest-guardian boy (he/him) with messy brown hair, green eyes, golden deer antlers with small green leaves, heavy steel-and-gold plate armour with a white fur collar, a green scarf, a green tabard with a gold leaf emblem and a tattered green cape, holding a grey stone war hammer with gold bands on a wooden handle and a tall rectangular dark-green tower shield with gold riveted trim, a gold tree emblem and a green gem, standing in the showcase pose facing right'
ENT1='his entrance from the earth (Frame 1 shows no character yet). Frame 1: a jagged crack opens in the ground where he will stand and the tips of a few thick brown roots poke up out of it. Frame 2: thick brown roots and green vines burst up out of the crack, twisting around each other, waist high. Frame 3: the roots twist higher into a stocky tree-trunk cocoon of rough brown bark the size and shape of the hero with his tall shield, a few green leaves sprouting from its top. Frame 4: the bark cocoon is complete, a bright split cracks open down its middle. Frame 5: the bark splits apart into two halves and he steps out between them, shield first, the antlers showing. Frame 6: the bark halves fall back and sink into the ground, he stands in front, a few big green leaves falling around him. Frame 7: the roots have withdrawn into the ground, two or three big leaves drifting past his feet. Frame 8: nothing but the hero, standing exactly in the pose of Image 1. Every cell keeps a clear empty magenta margin on all four sides: the roots, the bark and the tree never touch or cross the cell edges or reach into the neighbouring cell, and nothing is taller than the hero with his antlers.'
NECK1='he rolls his neck: tilts his head to one side with eyes closed (frame 2), rolls it over to the other side (frame 3), then heaves the stone war hammer up and rests it on his right shoulder with a satisfied grin (frames 4-5), holds it there (frame 6), and lowers it back down to its resting place (frame 7). The tower shield stays planted, feet stay planted. He keeps exactly the same size and place as Image 1 in every frame.'
